From 6c6a1b1936e0ff75738680f4a8968cff5055ffd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] fix(data): crash-free decoding, codegen-friendly
 schema, payment and R7 checks (verifier round 1)

- clip messages by grapheme clusters (was: byte slices inside UTF-8)
- nesting cap before the descent; format versions beyond 9 digits; dates
  of the years 1-9899, terms days <= 36500, texts <= 10000 characters
- document types exactly as invoice() accepts them (self-billed credit
  note = 261); required texts and lines must not be blank
- cross-field rules as dependentSchemas (TS/Rust generators get usable
  types); exact positive percent patterns; optional "" and null per 3.3
- payment: details of another method, credit-note guards and a transfer
  without account become data issues when hydrated
- near-miss data input keys panic; BOM for YAML; 0.15 path by extension
- result: ASCII minus, paid totals, BT-121 code, two-decimal money
- modifier without a VAT group: data issue when hydrated; frame.typ
  one-line ellipsis bugfix
- decoder hot path: precomputed dispatch, inline rows (0.15-0.27 ms/row)
- payment root export as a lazy facade; signature test checks classes
  and runs on 0.14

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RaaQussN1QVEE8zRWeeCD3
